{
  "item": "Tree01",
  "mu_name": "Tree",
  "mu_name_from": "Lorencia's object slot 0. WorldObjectCatalog.cs runs the world's types as named blocks and Tree is the first, thirteen of them from 0, so Tree01.bmd is object type 0 - the first thing in the first town's table.",
  "world": "lorencia",
  "object_type": 0,
  "why_this_one": "The most-placed object in Lorencia and the case the world profile was really written for. Two sheets, one of them a cut-out, and both of them tiling - the trunk wraps its bark round itself and the canopy is a handful of cards. It is also the first asset where the cut-out sheet is the larger half of the model rather than a garnish: 144 of its 412 triangles are leaves.",
  "profile": "world",
  "sheets": {
    "tree": "tree.png",
    "tree_a": "tree_a.png"
  },
  "sheet_from": "Data/Object1/tree.OZJ (128x128) and Tree_a.OZT (128x128), both from MuMain. The .bmd names tree.jpg and Tree_a.tga.",
  "sheet_materials": {
    "tree": "bark",
    "tree_a": "foliage"
  },
  "material_note": "Per sheet, which is what the tiled path made possible: tree.jpg is furrowed bark wherever it appears and Tree_a.tga is a leaf canopy. No island had to be looked at.",
  "cutout": [
    "tree_a"
  ],
  "cutout_from": "Tree_a.OZT carries a real alpha channel cutting away 48% of its square. Declared rather than sniffed, for the reason in tests/cutouts.py.",
